---
title: ForegroundLossRecovery
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> Preparing
  Preparing --> Requested : Request
  Requested --> GraphReady : GraphReady [mapped]
  GraphReady --> Serving : Serve / retire intent, lock
  Preparing --> Dead : Die
  Requested --> Dead : Die
  GraphReady --> Dead : Die
  Serving --> Dead : Die
  Dead --> Lost : Watch / release lock
  Dead --> Lost : StartFails / same message
  state advice <<choice>>
  Lost --> advice
  advice --> Inspect : [fresh up, Requested]
  advice --> Down : [run recorded]
  advice --> Up : [fresh up, Preparing]
  Down --> Up : down --recover
  Up --> Recovered : hack up
  Inspect --> [*]
  Recovered --> [*]

  note right of Preparing
    Images, review, restore
    selection; nothing requested.
    A restart holds its lock.
  end note
  note right of GraphReady
    Ready and mapped. A restart
    still holds its cleaned
    intent and its lock.
  end note
  note right of Dead
    The watch and the start's
    own error race; both print
    the stage message.
  end note
  note left of Inspect
    A fresh up has no record
    for down to retire yet:
    none named.
    INV NoNeedlessWithholding
  end note
  note right of Down
    Starts the pool; retires a
    lost start or a ready run,
    port or none, data kept.
    Removes containers a lost
    VM brought back.
  end note
  note right of Recovered
    INV NoRefusedAdvice
    Every named command is
    accepted, for up and restart.
  end note

  classDef live stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef wait stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef ok stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef fail stroke-width:1.6px
  classDef idle stroke-width:1.6px
  class Preparing,Requested,GraphReady wait
  class Serving live
  class Dead,Lost fail
  class Down,Up wait
  class Recovered ok
  class Inspect idle
